  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to the `OrderPlaced` event, but I kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` instead of renaming them. Renaming them outright would go against ARCH-4 in CLAUDE.md. billing-service and analytics-ingest both read this event from other repos, and the rule says renames have to go through deprecation so deployed consumers keep working.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** every `OrderPlaced` event now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`. `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still there with the same values, marked `@deprecated` with a note pointing to the new names. Existing consumers keep working, and new ones can use the names the Payments and Customer APIs use.\n- **Tests:** updated to check both the new and the old fields, including in the serialized Kafka payload.\n- `npm test` passes (39/39) and `npm run arch` reports no new violations. It still lists one known violation that it ignores; I didn't change that.\n\n**What I left alone**\n- **`schemaVersion` is still 3.** Adding fields shouldn't break anyone, and changing the version number could trip a consumer that checks for exactly 3. If your versioning policy says new fields need a version bump, tell me and I'll change it.\n- **The HTTP response** (`POST /orders`, `GET /orders/{id}`) still returns `placedAt` and `totalCents`. You asked about the event only, and ARCH-8 requires that response to stay compatible for web-storefront.\n\n**To finish the rename**\n1. Get billing-service and analytics-ingest to switch to `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n2. Once both are deployed, remove the deprecated fields. Your versioning policy may require a schema version bump for that.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
